## Preconditions

Do not deploy until required PR checks pass, the reviewed commit is on the intended branch, the promotion archive and SHA-256 exist, its GitHub provenance attestation verifies, the target environment is configured, and the accountable human authorizes that environment.

## Preview

Run `Deploy preview` manually with the successful quality-run ID, full commit SHA, expected archive digest, and a validated isolated Worker name. Preview credentials must be separate from production. Treat preview content and URLs as public.

## Staging

Promote the same archive with `Deploy staging`. Verify its signed provenance and digest before extraction. Run `Post-deploy verification` with `environment` set to `staging`, commit, and artifact digest. The workflow records redacted promotion and verification evidence.

## Production

Run `Deploy production` only from `main` after staging verification. The workflow verifies that the requested commit belongs to `main`, downloads the exact tested archive, verifies attestation and digest, and deploys under the production environment gate. It does not rebuild. The job records approval-boundary and promotion evidence only after the environment gate releases it.

## Verification and evidence

Run `Post-deploy verification` separately for staging and production against each exact HTTPS URL. Correlate workflow URL, commit SHA, archive digest, environment, result, and any incident ID. Never record credentials or submitted contact data.

## Stop conditions

Stop on a missing approval, missing or mismatched digest, failing required check, unknown commit, unavailable rollback access, unexpected secret request, failed header check, or unhealthy customer path.

## Activation note

The workflows and evidence validators are implemented. They have not yet produced a verified attestation or staging/production deployment record. Production currently lacks a required reviewer and permits administrator bypass, so the external approval gate is not complete.
